# TODO - User-supplied DOOM source interoperability generator

## Objective

Consume the accepted normalized DOOM source tree produced by `quality.rs` and use
`interop/algorithms/amalgamate.rs` to emit one deterministic
`interop/algorithms/out/doom_amalgamated.c`. Resolve translation-unit boundaries,
internal-linkage collisions, preprocessing environments, includes, declarations,
and provenance through pinned Clang before admitting the single-file artifact.

## Acceptance

- `amalgamate.rs` consumes only the normalized generated tree and never rewrites
  the user-owned source tree directly.
- Translation-unit semantics, internal linkage, macro environments, declaration
  ordering, and required provenance survive deterministic aggregation.
- Plain textual concatenation and source-specific hand patches are not accepted
  implementations of amalgamation.
- The normalized multi-file build and the amalgamated native build are compared
  differentially before admission.
- The accepted `doom_amalgamated.c` is copied byte-for-byte to
  `tests/applications/doom/out/doom.c` for the end-to-end pipeline fixture.
- Evidence is durable enough to move this TODO to `docs/todo/completed/` and
  remove the exact TODO heading without losing unfinished intent.

## Evidence

- Expected durable artifact surface: `interop/algorithms/amalgamate.rs`,
  `interop/algorithms/out/doom_fixed/`,
  `interop/algorithms/out/doom_amalgamated.c`,
  `tests/applications/doom/out/doom.c`.
- Required evidence: normalized/amalgamated manifests, deterministic hashes,
  native differential traces, and provenance mapping.
- Prerequisite completion evidence: `doom-quality-and-modernization-pass`,
  `clang-c-frontend-integration`, `reuse-shar-legal-and-interoperability-corpus`.